---
import ResourceArticle from "@/layouts/ResourceArticle.astro";
import { resources } from "@/lib/resources";
---
<ResourceArticle page={resources.spotlight}>
  <p>For a quick calculation, press Spotlight’s default shortcut, <kbd>Command–Space</kbd>, and type <code>144/12</code> to see <strong>12</strong> in the search window. You can enter a conversion the same way, such as <code>25 cm in inches</code>.</p>
  <p>When you’re working through several calculations in a spreadsheet, it helps to keep the expression and result in view as you move between cells. EvaBar has a floating panel you can pin above the spreadsheet for that workflow.</p>

  <h2>Spotlight and EvaBar compared</h2>
  <table class="resource-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Spotlight</th><th scope="col">EvaBar</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Default shortcut</th><td><kbd>Command–Space</kbd></td><td><kbd>Control–Shift–Space</kbd>. You can also click the menu bar icon.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Where results appear</th><td>In the Spotlight search window.</td><td>In a floating panel you can pin above your workspace.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Calculations</th><td>Math expressions and conversions for currency, temperature, and measurements.</td><td>Math expressions with functions such as <code>avg()</code> and <code>log()</code>. Press <kbd>Return</kbd> to copy the result.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Setup</th><td>Built into macOS.</td><td>Free, open-source app for macOS 13 or later.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="resource-source">See Apple’s guide to <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/guide/mac-help/mchldd6ba066/mac">calculations and conversions in Spotlight</a>.</p>

  <h2>Calculate an average for each spreadsheet row</h2>
  <p>Suppose each row needs the average of three measurements. With the spreadsheet open, bring up EvaBar and click the lock to pin it. Enter <code>avg(12,18,24)</code> and press <kbd>Return</kbd> to copy <strong>18</strong>.</p>
  <p>Click the cell that needs the result and paste it. The pinned panel stays visible, so you can click back into the expression field and enter the measurements for the next row.</p>
</ResourceArticle>
